# The bench's addresses. Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored, as
# bench.local.md is, because these are host-specific and belong in no
# commit. Anything already in the environment beats the file.
#
#   BRIDGE  the UNO through the Pi's serial bridge, host:port. From the
#           workstation that is the Pi; on the Pi itself, 127.0.0.1:6545.
#   SCOPE   the oscilloscope's address, without a port (SCPI is 5555).
#   PI      user@host for the tools that run something over there: the
#           eye (tools/eye.py), the rig check, the bring-up on the Pi.
#
# Used by tools/bench-check.py, tools/rig-check.py and scripts/hands-*.sh.
BRIDGE=nesbench:6545
SCOPE=192.0.2.10
PI=you@nesbench
